X. The United Kingdom: Sovereignty and Interoperability

The British case presents another interesting paradox.

The United Kingdom possesses a globally important currency and sophisticated financial infrastructure.

A digital pound could therefore become not merely a domestic payment instrument but a potential component of future international settlement.

The central strategic question is whether digital currencies become isolated national technologies or interoperable components of global finance.

A LIGDI model would allow Britain to preserve:

