XIV. The LIGDI Architecture

A theoretical LIGDI system could contain several layers.

Layer 1: Sovereign Issuance

Each central bank controls its own CBDC.

[
CB_i \rightarrow CBDC_i
]

Layer 2: Identity

A privacy-preserving identity layer determines whether participants are authorized to transact.

Layer 3: Settlement

LIGDI provides the distributed settlement environment.

Layer 4: Foreign Exchange

Algorithms and regulated liquidity providers facilitate currency conversion.

Layer 5: Smart Contracts

Programmable contracts automate legitimate financial processes.

Layer 6: Governance

An international governance structure establishes protocol rules without controlling national monetary policy.

The architecture therefore resembles:

[
\boxed{
Sovereignty
+
Interoperability
+
Security
+
Programmability
}
]

