XX. Governance of LIGDI

A global financial blockchain would require extraordinarily sophisticated governance.

A hypothetical structure could include:

Sovereign Council

Central banks and monetary authorities participate in governance.

Technical Council

Cryptographers, distributed-systems engineers and cybersecurity experts maintain the protocol.

Legal Council

International financial-law experts establish standards for cross-border settlement.

Privacy Council

Independent experts evaluate civil-liberties and data-protection implications.

Emergency Council

A narrowly defined mechanism handles catastrophic technical incidents.

Governance should be:

[
Multilateral + Transparent + Auditable + Limited
]

rather than concentrated in a single state or corporation.

