XXIV. The Imperative

Governments should therefore stop asking only:

“Should we launch a CBDC?”

They should ask:

“What architecture should CBDCs collectively form?”

The first question is national.

The second is civilizational.

A fragmented CBDC world could reproduce the weaknesses of today’s fragmented international payment infrastructure.

An interoperable CBDC world could create an entirely new monetary architecture.

The difference could be enormous.

If:

